{"reference":"Ezekiel 23","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":23,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"A difficult allegory","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The chapter portrays Samaria and Jerusalem as two women through sexualized marriage, prostitution, exposure, and punishment imagery. This rhetoric is central to the chapter’s argument, but it is also ethically disturbing; the cities are personified through language that makes their judgment graphic and gendered.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 23:1-49"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_023_4a514ccb82df39dc8ad30602"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}